    "question": {
      ":question/id": "97a5b63d-3797-59e3-994e-40242369d01a",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
